# KNOWN GAP — LIVE MEMORY-SAFETY DEFECT AT HEAD, reachable by changing ONE
# TOKEN in a committed, passing fixture.
#
# `tests/fixtures/box_trait_struct_field.gg:23` reads:
#     Holder h = Holder(Box.new(Robot("R2")))     -> rc 0, prints R2
# Change the constructor spelling and nothing else:
#     Holder h = Holder(Box(Robot("R2")))         -> rc 1 on BOTH lanes
#         C    : gorget: panic: gorget_string_free invariant: cap=688948
#         LLVM : gorget: panic: gorget_string_free invariant: cap=4
#
# ASan: heap-use-after-free -- freed by `__gorget_box_free_Robot` from `main`,
# then re-read via `Holder__drop -> Box__Robot__drop -> Robot__drop`.
# Two owners, one allocation.
#
# THE WRITER (Core #1 -- fix at the write site):
# `pack_trait_object_for_smart_ptr_ctor` (`src/ir/lowering/exprs/calls.rs:989-1041`)
# emits `_4 = copy _3` at `:1039` and NEVER CONSUMES THE SOURCE -- no
# `move_zero`, no `drops.unregister`. ONE producer, 12 call sites.
#
# ⚠ FORMATION-SPECIFIC (do not widen the claim): the struct-field constructor
# argument position crashes; a vector-literal formation is clean; two other
# formations reject the bare spelling outright.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE MIRROR OF `box_new_discarded_trait_pack_leak.gg`. The two are
# one root seen from both sides and MUST be fixed together:
#     * bare `Box(...)`  REGISTERS the value and double-frees through the pack.
#     * `Box.new(...)`   does NOT register and LEAKS.
# The pair is its own positive control, and it settles the fix shape: register
# at birth (the bare spelling is RIGHT to register) AND make the pack CONSUME
# its source. Deleting the registration to make the suite green is the wrong
# fix -- it converts this crash into the sibling's leak.
#
# INTENDED (asserted below): prints R2 on BOTH backends, ASan-clean.
# Measured 2026-08-27 at HEAD by R45 Track A brief-review pass 12;
# orchestrator-verified on both lanes against the committed fixture.

#
# ⚠⚠ "ASan-CLEAN" IN THE INTENDED CLAUSE ABOVE IS RETRACTED (2026-08-27).
# It is measurably unreachable: under the full fix a 3-byte residual remains on
# EVERY trait-dispatching row (the vtable-thunk String return), and
# Mutex/Shared payloads leak 65 B before AND after through a separate
# runtime-ABI gap (GorgetMutex has no payload-drop fn pointer at all).
#
# CORRECTED INTENT: eliminate the double-free / mint leak this fixture names,
# and leave NO NEW sanitizer finding -- measured as a DELTA against a HEAD
# baseline captured on the SAME program, not as absolute silence. Absolute
# ASan silence is a separate, larger objective owed by t0700 + the thunk leak
# + the Mutex/Shared ABI gap together.
#
# ⚠ `security_safe_no_leak` (tests/security.rs:261-280) rejects ANY sanitizer
# output, so a net wired to it cannot express a delta.
trait Speaker:
    String speak(self)

struct Robot:
    String name

equip Robot with Speaker:
    String speak(self):
        return self.name

struct Holder:
    Box[Speaker] s

void main():
    Holder h = Holder(Box(Robot("R2")))
    print(h.s.speak())
